# Normalize all text files to LF line endings — in the repository and on
# checkout — regardless of platform or the user's global git config.
#
# Why: Atelier's build scripts run inside a Linux container (Docker
# quick-launch bind-mounts the host checkout straight into /studio). If a
# Windows checkout converts them to CRLF, the container fails on them with
# "bad interpreter: .../bash^M". This setting overrides core.autocrlf so
# every checkout — lean install, Docker, GitHub Codespaces — gets the same
# LF files, and `git status` stays clean across all of them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files — never subject to any line-ending conversion.
# (.eps is deliberately left off this list: this project's cover/QR EPS
# files are plain ASCII PostScript, not a binary preview format, so they
# normalize safely as text like everything else.)
*.docx binary
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.ico  binary
